WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.229
- [Narrator] Fire
stations, big red trucks,

00:00:02.229 --> 00:00:03.371
flashing sirens,

00:00:03.371 --> 00:00:05.777
that cool shiny pole,

00:00:05.777 --> 00:00:07.971
well, it all dates back to colonial times

00:00:07.971 --> 00:00:10.960
and this guy had a little
something to do with it.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.379
That's right.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.462
Ben Franklin.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.701
Most known for the Constitution,

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.861
electricity and the bifocals,

00:00:19.861 --> 00:00:24.061
Ben Franklin had a weird
obsession with fire safety.

00:00:24.061 --> 00:00:25.192
On a trip to Massachusetts,

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:26.999
Franklin noticed that
the good people of Boston

00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:28.280
were much more fire savvy

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.718
than his fellow citizens in Philadelphia.

00:00:30.718 --> 00:00:32.312
This got Ben thinking

00:00:32.312 --> 00:00:33.391
and he came up with the idea

00:00:33.391 --> 00:00:35.421
to create a club or society

00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:38.311
of active men belonging
to each fire engine

00:00:38.311 --> 00:00:39.960
whose business is to attend

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.781
all fires with it whenever they happen.

00:00:42.781 --> 00:00:44.240
Then Ben got weird,

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.491
he wrote an anonymous letter

00:00:45.491 --> 00:00:47.109
to his own newspaper

00:00:47.109 --> 00:00:48.280
as a senior citizen titled,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.667
‘Protections of Towns from Fire.’

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:53.229
“Dear Pennsylvania Gazette…”

00:00:53.229 --> 00:00:55.851
The letter encouraged a
better fire safety plan

00:00:55.851 --> 00:00:58.019
and painted a horrifying alternative.

00:00:58.019 --> 00:00:59.227
People jumping out of windows,

00:00:59.227 --> 00:01:00.469
breaking their necks

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:02.800
and being burned alive.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.131
But it worked.

00:01:04.131 --> 00:01:07.309
In 1736, the first American
volunteer fire department

00:01:07.309 --> 00:01:08.379
was born.

00:01:08.379 --> 00:01:09.819
The Union Fire Company.

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:11.891
It was comprised of 30 volunteers

00:01:11.891 --> 00:01:13.930
and you might know some of them.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.160
George Washington,

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:15.993
Thomas Jefferson,

00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:17.811
and Samuel Adams.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:18.644
That's right.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:19.477
Our Founding Fathers

00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:22.169
were also firefighters.

00:01:22.169 --> 00:01:23.509
Soon after fire companies

00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:25.960
and clubs sprang up all over Philadelphia

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.269
and then across the 13 colonies.

00:01:28.269 --> 00:01:30.539
So, thanks to the matchless leadership

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:32.016
of Benjamin Franklin,

00:01:32.016 --> 00:01:34.099
we now have firefighters.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.347
Thanks, Ben.

